  "articlePanels": [
    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Care homes and schools use cleaning and maintenance products where vulnerable people live or learn. The COSHH Regulations 2002 apply. Here is what to assess.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>The employer assesses every hazardous product staff use, in a care home, nursery or school.</li><li>HSE asks you to consider other people affected, which here means residents, children and visitors.</li><li>Cleaning chemicals, disinfectants, laundry products and maintenance products are the usual list.</li><li>Biological agents, such as infection from soiled items, are also in scope of COSHH.</li><li>Quickler files a COSHH Record per product. It does not replace your competent person.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The rule",
      "heading": "Who is responsible",
      "html": "<p>The employer. For a care home that is the provider. For a school it is the employer of the staff, such as the council, trust or governing body. <a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2002/2677/contents\">the COSHH Regulations 2002</a> cover the products and the biological agents staff meet. <a href=\"https://www.hse.gov.uk/coshh/basics/assessment.htm\">HSE: how to carry out a COSHH risk assessment</a> asks you to consider people other than staff who may be harmed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The products",
      "heading": "What to assess",
      "html": "<p><strong>Care homes:</strong> cleaning and disinfectant products, laundry chemicals, products used in the kitchen, and maintenance products. Infection from soiled items and clinical waste is a biological hazard to control as well.</p><p><strong>Schools:</strong> the caretaker's and cleaners' products, grounds and maintenance products, and science, art and design and technology stores. See HSE's pages under <a href=\"https://www.hse.gov.uk/coshh/industry/index.htm\">HSE: COSHH and your industry</a>.</p>"
    },
