      "html": "<h3>Do care homes need COSHH assessments?</h3><p>Yes. The provider is the employer, and staff use hazardous cleaning and maintenance products and meet biological agents.</p><h3>Do schools need COSHH assessments?</h3><p>Yes. The employer assesses products used by caretakers, cleaners and teaching staff, and considers pupils who may be affected.</p><h3>Who is at risk besides staff?</h3><p>HSE asks you to consider others affected. In a care home that is residents and visitors. In a school it is pupils and visitors.</p><h3>How do I show an inspector the assessments?</h3><p>Keep one Record per product in one list. Quickler Records come back in your own Word form.</p><h3>Does Quickler cover medicines?</h3><p>No. This page and the COSHH Check cover hazardous products such as cleaners and chemicals.</p>"
