s or processes change.</p><h2>A Record for each product</h2><p>Start your COSHH Check in WhatsApp, send the safety data sheet and say who uses the product, for how long and how often, and where. Quickler files a Record named after the product, in your own Word form, ready for an inspector or a visit. Every Record sits in one list, with an audit trail of who changed what and when.</p><p>It does not write the assessment for you. Write 10 COSHH records a month and that's £7.50 a record; at 30 a month it is £2.50 a record. Reports, photos and messages are unlimited. See <a href=\"/pages/care-home-health-safety-audit-uk.html\">care home health and safety audits</a>, <a href=\"/pages/school-health-safety-audit-uk.html\">school health and safety audits</a> and the <a href=\"/pages/coshh-risk-assessment-field-teams-uk.html\">COSHH guide</a>.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do care homes need COSHH assessments?</h3><p>Yes. The provider is the employer, and staff use hazardous cleaning and maintenance products and meet biological agents.</p><h3>Do schools need COSHH assessments?</h3><p>Yes. The employer assesses products used by caretakers, cleaners and teaching staff, and considers pupils who may be affected.</p><h3>Who is at risk besides staff?</h3><p>HSE asks you to consider others affected. In a care home that is residents and visitors. In a school it is pupils and visitors.</p><h3>How do I show an inspector the assessments?</h3><p>Keep one Record per product in one list. Quickler Records come back in your own Word form.</p><h3>Does Quickler cover medicines?</h3><p>No. This page and the COSHH Check cover hazardous products such as cleaners and chemicals.</p>",
